  "support_contract": "Synthetic feature space is exactly the listed bins, with deterministic prediction pair equal to each bin. Bins absent from a scenario are structural support exclusions, not observed-zero exclusions. Every listed bin is retained in confidence construction, including zero-count bins.",
  "assumptions": "Fixed classifiers; independent class-stratified source and target evidence. rho is a prespecified sensitivity allowance, not estimated from target labels or unlabeled evidence.",
  "decision_rule": "ADAPT if verified conservative lower>1e-10, FREEZE if upper<-1e-10, otherwise ABSTAIN. Failed and infeasible LPs abstain.",
  "family_scope": "Each fixed pair and rho invocation has alpha=.05 conditional on the declared transport class. No simultaneous claim over sample-size/rho/scenario grid; budgets are prespecified sensitivity analyses, not post-outcome selection.",
  "analysis": [
    "Report every arm and regime; no best-rho selection or target-driven tuning.",
    "Paired LP and separate-accuracy relaxation use identical probability-table constraints. Plugin is minimum-norm constrained-equation approximation with negative components clipped and normalized, descriptive only.",
    "Wrong direction includes strict action at zero true benefit using 1e-12 reporting tolerance. ABSTAIN takes frozen model for regret calculations.",
    "Intervals absent after solver failure count as not containing truth. Plugin inclusion and width are null.",
    "Per-regime Monte Carlo 95 percent CP intervals are descriptive, not simultaneous; conditional false adapt is null when no ADAPT occurs.",
    "Matched evidence worlds share source counts and target marginal counts by evidence_group seed. Target truth is a separate score stream excluded from decision interface.",
    "Retain all numerical failures and assumption-violation wrong decisions.",
    "Decision latency is combined three-arm CPU time and excludes adaptation."
  ],
